🧠 What we have actually built

Our architecture now starts looking like:

Healthcare Traffic
        │
        ▼
Traffic Generator
        │
        ▼
Traffic Classifier
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Traffic Type            │
│ ECG / ICU / EHR / etc.  │
└────────────┬────────────┘
             │
             ▼
     Criticality Score
             │
             ▼
       Routing Engine

The routing engine isn't using the score yet.

That's intentional.

We're building the system in layers so that later we can measure exactly what each addition contributes.

⚠️ Important: this is not the final classifier

For the research/patent version, eventually we should not simply say:

if ECG → 5

We can later make the criticality score depend on multiple features such as:

Patient criticality
+
Traffic type
+
Emergency status
+
Latency requirement
+
Packet loss sensitivity
+
Current network congestion

For example:

Criticality Score
=
w1(Patient Severity)
+
w2(Traffic Type)
+
w3(Emergency Status)
+
w4(Latency Sensitivity)

That will be much stronger academically.

But Step 10 establishes the baseline healthcare classification layer first.

